[PASS] a reachable target running a mutation driver is armed
[PASS] the driver may be reached through a make variable ($(PY) x.py)
[PASS] a driver on a target the entry never runs is not an arm
[PASS] ...until the processor's CI names that target
[PASS] a compile-time mutation define a recipe passes is armed
[PASS] a mutation define reaches the recipe through variable expansion
[PASS] a negative-case table the recipe consumes is armed
[PASS] a DUT-rewriting driver with no table is still a driver
[PASS] a DUT reader that rewrites nothing is not a driver
[PASS] (A) a suite whose entry runs nothing is not armed
[PASS] (B) a comment naming mutants.py is not an arm
[PASS] (C) an unrelated -DUSE_MUTEX define is not an arm, even when passed
[PASS] (D) an empty mutants: target is not an arm
[PASS] (E) README prose about a negative arm is not an arm
[PASS] (F) a comment mentioning --selftest is not an arm
[PASS] a driver named as an echo argument is not run, so not an arm
[PASS] a table variable nobody's recipe consumes is not an arm
[PASS] mutation prose alone is not an executable arm
[PASS] a comment marker inside the driver does not make it one
[PASS] (G) a `-` recipe line ignores errors: `-python3 mutants.py` is not an arm
[PASS] (H) `python3 mutants.py || true` is not an arm: the fallback masks the driver
[PASS] `|| :` and `|| echo ...` mask the same way
[PASS] a `-` on another line of the same target leaves the driver's line evidence
[PASS] an && chain carries the driver's failure, so it still counts
[PASS] `@-` and `-@` are both the ignore prefix, before and after expansion
[PASS] a `; true` tail masks; `set -e` restores the driver's failure, `set +e` drops it
[PASS] a driver feeding a pipe reports the consumer's status, not its own
[PASS] a fallback that re-raises (`|| exit 1`, `|| { ...; exit 1; }`) still counts
[PASS] an if condition, a $$(...) and a backtick substitution are not arms
[PASS] .IGNORE makes a target's, or every, recipe non-evidence
[PASS] the entry reader sees the loop, the named target and the sub-make
[PASS] an unseeded draw is caught
[PASS] a seeded draw is not
[PASS] a Random(seed) instance counts as seeded
[PASS] the guide's TEST_SEED pattern is clean
[PASS] an unseeded random.Random() instance draw is caught
[PASS] a SystemRandom draw is caught (it cannot be seeded)
[PASS] from random import randint is caught
[PASS] ...and seeded through seed() is not
[PASS] random.choices and random.gauss are draws
[PASS] np.random draws are caught
[PASS] ...and np.random.seed / default_rng(seed) make them replayable
[PASS] secrets.randbelow is a draw that can never be seeded
[PASS] secrets.token_hex is a nonce, not a draw (known limit)
[PASS] a file that never draws is not counted
[PASS] a C rand() with no srand is caught
[PASS] a C rand() with srand is not
[PASS] std::rand() is caught
[PASS] srand(time(NULL)) is not a recorded seed
[PASS] mt19937(random_device) is caught
[PASS] ...unless the seed it produced is recorded
[PASS] a literally seeded engine is deterministic
[PASS] $urandom with no seed is caught
[PASS] $urandom_range and $random are caught
[PASS] randomize() is a draw
[PASS] srandom(seed) makes SystemVerilog draws replayable
[PASS] $urandom(seed) is a seeded draw
[PASS] a +seed plusarg records the seed
[PASS] a draw in a comment is not a draw
[PASS] a draw inside a string literal is not a draw
